    "show_share": true,
    "description": "As if being a teenager is not difficult enough, adolescents living in Northern Nigeria have to worry about social restrictions, poor socio-economic conditions and the threat of Boko Haram attacks. This is the reality of several young men and women who live in Northern Nigeria. According to a  World Bank report  (2016), this region has the highest infant and maternal mortality rate in the country as well as the lowest rate of child enrolment in schools, the highest number of unemployed young people and the highest levels of poverty in Nigeria.",
